          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "note": "Note 3: Operating Segments",
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "material_event",
            "content": "We previously announced the organizational change to integrate AXG into CCG and DCAI. This change is intended to drive a more effective go-to-market capability and to accelerate the scale of these businesses, while also reducing costs. As a result, we modified our segment reporting in the first quarter of 2023 to align to this and certain other business reorganizations.",
            "entity_name": "Intel AXG Integration into CCG and DCAI",
            "entity_type_entity": "MaterialEvent",
            "valid_from": "2024-01-25",
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "note": "Note 4: Non-Controlling Interests",
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "material_event",
            "content": "In 2022, we closed a transaction with Brookfield Asset Management (Brookfield) resulting in the formation of Arizona Fab LLC (Arizona Fab), a VIE that we consolidate into our financial statements because we are the primary beneficiary. Generally, contributions will be made to, and distributions will be received from, Arizona Fab based on both parties' proportional ownership. We will be the sole operator of two new chip factories that will be constructed by Arizona Fab, and we will have the right to purchase 100% of the related factory output. We have an unrecognized commitment to fund our respective share of the total construction costs of Arizona Fab of $29.0 billion.",
            "entity_name": "Arizona Fab LLC Formation with Brookfield Asset Management",
            "entity_type_entity": "MaterialEvent",
            "valid_from": "2024-01-25",
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "note": "Note 4: Non-Controlling Interests",
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "material_event",
            "content": "During the second quarter of 2023, we converted 38.5 million of our Mobileye Class B shares into Class A shares, representing 5% of Mobileye's outstanding capital stock, and subsequently sold the Class A shares for $42 per share as part of a secondary offering, receiving net proceeds of $1.6 billion and increasing our capital in excess of par value by $663 million, net of tax.",
            "entity_name": "Mobileye 2023 Secondary Share Offering",
            "entity_type_entity": "MaterialEvent",
            "valid_from": "2024-01-25",
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "note": "Note 4: Non-Controlling Interests",
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "material_event",
            "content": "In the third and fourth quarters of 2023, we closed agreements to sell a combined 32% minority stake in our IMS business, a business within our IFS operating segment —including a 20% stake to Bain Capital and a 10% stake to TSMC. Net proceeds resulting from the minority stake sales totaled $1.4 billion, and our capital in excess of par value increased by $958 million, net of tax.",
            "entity_name": "IMS Nanofabrication 32% Minority Stake Sale",
            "entity_type_entity": "MaterialEvent",
            "valid_from": "2024-01-25",
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "note": "Note 3: Operating Segments",
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "material_event",
            "content": "In 2022, we initiated the wind-down of our Intel Optane memory business, which is part of our DCAI operating segment. While Intel Optane is a leading technology, it was not aligned to our strategic priorities. Separately, we continue to embrace the CXL standard. As a result, we recognized an inventory impairment of $723 million in cost of sales on the Consolidated Statements of Income in 2022.",
            "entity_name": "Intel Optane Memory Business Wind-Down",
            "entity_type_entity": "MaterialEvent",
            "valid_from": "2024-01-25",
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "note": "Note 2: Accounting Policies",
              "section_type": "Item_8"
            },
            "chunk_type": "material_event",
            "content": "Effective January 2023, the estimated useful lives of certain machinery and equipment in our wafer fabrication facilities were increased from 5 to 8 years. This change in estimate was applied prospectively beginning in the first quarter of 2023.",
            "entity_name": "Intel Wafer Fab Equipment Useful Life Extension",
            "entity_type_entity": "MaterialEvent",
            "valid_from": "2024-01-25",
            "valid_until": null
          },
          {
            "attributes": {
              "note": "Consolidated Statements of Stockholders' Equity",
              "section_type": "Item_8",
              "unit": "millions_usd"
            },
            "chunk_type": "capital_return",
            "content": "Cash dividends declared ($0.74 per share of common stock)— ——(3,088)— (3,088)",
            "entity_name": "INTC FY2023 Cash Dividend",
            "entity_type_entity": "CapitalReturn",
